1
00:00:47,422 --> 00:00:50,383
I'm never going back
to that life, Mama Yaya.

2
00:00:50,467 --> 00:00:51,718
Are you happy?

3
00:00:51,801 --> 00:00:54,220
- This is my life now.
- Chiara.

4
00:00:54,304 --> 00:00:56,806
This is the life I chose.

5
00:00:59,893 --> 00:01:01,519
What do you mean "congratulations"?

6
00:01:01,603 --> 00:01:03,146
Don't you remember?

7
00:01:15,408 --> 00:01:17,994
Let's see who you're hiding, Sean.

8
00:01:33,676 --> 00:01:38,681
<i>anyone who tries</i>
<i>to mess with our lives again.</i>

9
00:01:59,327 --> 00:02:00,620
It's time.

10
00:02:25,019 --> 00:02:28,481
<i>But what if Chiara still has</i>
<i>unfinished business at La Concordat?</i>

11
00:02:28,565 --> 00:02:30,942
<i>Could that be why someone</i>
<i>still wants to reach out to her?</i>

12
00:02:41,661 --> 00:02:47,667
<i>No, Chiara isn't like that.</i>
<i>She's changed so much.</i>

13
00:02:49,836 --> 00:02:51,546
<i>I've seen how happy she is.</i>

14
00:02:52,589 --> 00:02:55,550
<i>How much she loves</i>
<i>the life they've built here.</i>

15
00:02:55,633 --> 00:02:57,218
<i>She wouldn't let anyone destroy that.</i>

16
00:02:58,845 --> 00:03:01,431
<i>If she did have unfinished business,</i>

17
00:03:01,514 --> 00:03:03,516
<i>she wouldn't be acting like this.</i>

18
00:03:04,100 --> 00:03:06,019
<i>Chiara is efficient,</i>

19
00:03:06,102 --> 00:03:06,936
<i>fast,</i>

20
00:03:07,020 --> 00:03:07,937
<i>quiet.</i>

21
00:03:14,777 --> 00:03:17,280
<i>Should I ask Chiara herself?</i>

22
00:03:19,657 --> 00:03:20,825
No.

23
00:03:25,580 --> 00:03:28,291
I'm only asking for one promise.

24
00:03:28,875 --> 00:03:31,419
I never stopped waiting

25
00:03:32,670 --> 00:03:35,298
and preparing for this day.

26
00:03:36,883 --> 00:03:40,094
The day our dreams
would finally come true.

27
00:03:45,308 --> 00:03:47,769
I've found a different dream.

28
00:03:48,269 --> 00:03:50,730
I've built the life I want.

29
00:03:52,774 --> 00:03:54,984
I did my part, Chiara.

30
00:03:56,110 --> 00:03:58,696
It's time for you to do yours.

31
00:04:13,628 --> 00:04:17,382
<i>The first time I saw you,</i>
<i>Chiara, I was shocked.</i>

32
00:04:18,967 --> 00:04:22,136
<i>I got used to seeing violence</i>
<i>in this mansion,</i>

33
00:04:22,220 --> 00:04:24,430
<i>but you were different.</i>

34
00:04:27,183 --> 00:04:30,353
<i>You never cried. You never complained.</i>

35
00:04:30,853 --> 00:04:34,899
<i>You just silently took</i>
<i>every hit and every beating.</i>

36
00:05:17,692 --> 00:05:18,526
Chiara.

37
00:05:19,610 --> 00:05:20,445
Chiara.

38
00:05:23,489 --> 00:05:24,699
My dear.

39
00:06:28,179 --> 00:06:29,263
So,

40
00:06:29,889 --> 00:06:31,682
I came here.

41
00:06:37,688 --> 00:06:39,232
Then you came along.

42
00:06:43,569 --> 00:06:46,864
I just wanted to take care of you.

43
00:06:59,043 --> 00:07:00,002
Yaya,

44
00:07:00,670 --> 00:07:02,088
Mama Yaya,

45
00:07:03,297 --> 00:07:04,966
while you're here.

46
00:07:15,143 --> 00:07:16,227
You know…

47
00:07:40,209 --> 00:07:41,669
I guess that's what it is.

48
00:07:42,295 --> 00:07:43,671
For now,

49
00:07:43,754 --> 00:07:46,299
La Morte Bianca is the queen.

50
00:07:49,260 --> 00:07:53,014
But one day,

51
00:07:53,097 --> 00:07:54,599
you could be the Queen.

52
00:08:08,946 --> 00:08:10,239
You too.

53
00:08:47,026 --> 00:08:49,695
I didn't even understand
what any of that meant.

54
00:08:50,738 --> 00:08:52,448
And so much has changed.

55
00:08:55,493 --> 00:08:58,454
I found a life I wanted to choose.

56
00:08:59,288 --> 00:09:01,874
And this is what I want now, not that.

57
00:09:04,293 --> 00:09:05,670
What do you think?

58
00:09:06,963 --> 00:09:09,882
You think everything that happened
in your life was just a coincidence?

59
00:09:10,841 --> 00:09:11,842
No, Chiara.

60
00:09:13,553 --> 00:09:15,846
There's a reason you're still alive.

61
00:09:16,597 --> 00:09:20,601
There's a reason La Morte Bianca fell.

62
00:09:21,352 --> 00:09:23,813
There's a reason you were left behind.

63
00:09:27,066 --> 00:09:28,859
What are you saying?

64
00:09:31,946 --> 00:09:34,282
I waited 20 years for you.

65
00:09:35,283 --> 00:09:39,870
For 20 years,
I prepared for this very moment.

66
00:09:43,249 --> 00:09:44,292
No.

67
00:09:49,297 --> 00:09:50,339
How?

68
00:09:51,841 --> 00:09:53,301
How could you be so sure

69
00:09:53,384 --> 00:09:54,969
that this day would come?

70
00:09:55,052 --> 00:09:56,971
That I'd still keep our promise,

71
00:09:57,054 --> 00:09:58,347
our plans?

72
00:09:59,056 --> 00:10:01,017
I didn't make sure.

73
00:10:01,100 --> 00:10:02,226
I prepared.

74
00:10:03,019 --> 00:10:06,897
While you thought
you were running away from the kingdom,

75
00:10:07,565 --> 00:10:11,110
I was slowly preparing this
for your return.

76
00:10:57,698 --> 00:10:59,992
<i>You know, sir,</i>
<i>the timing is just suspicious.</i>

77
00:11:00,493 --> 00:11:02,495
<i>Just a few days after Mikoy</i>
<i>proposed to Chiara,</i>

78
00:11:02,578 --> 00:11:04,038
<i>something like this suddenly came up.</i>

79
00:11:05,998 --> 00:11:08,459
I still haven't detected
any high-risk foreign nationals

80
00:11:08,542 --> 00:11:10,419
who entered the country this past week.

81
00:11:15,257 --> 00:11:17,593
I think this person is Filipino.

82
00:11:23,099 --> 00:11:25,059
There's something else you need to know.

83
00:11:33,067 --> 00:11:34,652
<i>When a leader is taken down,</i>

84
00:11:35,569 --> 00:11:37,405
<i>someone always takes their place.</i>

85
00:11:38,406 --> 00:11:41,867
<i>Our counterpart agencies</i>
<i>have noticed something.</i>

86
00:11:41,951 --> 00:11:44,620
<i>There have been more internal killings.</i>

87
00:11:44,703 --> 00:11:47,123
<i>More families are disappearing.</i>

88
00:11:47,706 --> 00:11:50,334
<i>And even their former allies</i>

89
00:11:51,127 --> 00:11:52,128
<i>are suddenly disappearing off the map.</i>

90
00:12:14,400 --> 00:12:16,861
There really wasn't another woman, babe.

91
00:12:16,944 --> 00:12:17,778
There really wasn't.

92
00:12:18,404 --> 00:12:19,738
Okay, even if you…

93
00:12:20,364 --> 00:12:21,782
even if you cut it off,

94
00:12:21,866 --> 00:12:23,784
you can fry it, chop it up,
make sisig out of it,

95
00:12:23,868 --> 00:12:24,743
there really wasn't anyone!

96
00:12:25,327 --> 00:12:27,580
There really wasn't. No one.

97
00:12:32,543 --> 00:12:34,295
No, I mean…

98
00:12:36,046 --> 00:12:39,133
That woman wasn't my ex.

99
00:12:39,216 --> 00:12:41,051
She wasn't someone from my past either.

100
00:12:41,135 --> 00:12:43,804
Okay, there really was nothing.
She wasn't a one-night stand either.

101
00:12:43,888 --> 00:12:45,514
There was nothing going on at all.

102
00:12:49,310 --> 00:12:51,437
- Sisig?
- Yes.

103
00:12:52,980 --> 00:12:54,231
And so?

104
00:12:59,570 --> 00:13:03,491
Something happened in my life
that became the most complicated chapter

105
00:13:03,574 --> 00:13:05,284
of my life, okay?

106
00:13:06,202 --> 00:13:08,496
I was completely broken that day.

107
00:13:09,788 --> 00:13:11,832
Then she suddenly came along.

108
00:13:12,458 --> 00:13:13,918
It's just… She was like

109
00:13:15,127 --> 00:13:16,545
a fairy godmother.

110
00:13:22,968 --> 00:13:24,261
But without a wand.

111
00:13:27,389 --> 00:13:30,518
She came into my life
at the worst possible time.

112
00:13:31,602 --> 00:13:32,770
She helped me.

113
00:13:34,104 --> 00:13:35,731
She helped me get back on my feet.

114
00:13:36,315 --> 00:13:37,399
That's all.

115
00:13:37,483 --> 00:13:39,860
There was nothing romantic about it.

116
00:13:44,281 --> 00:13:45,449
So,

117
00:13:46,408 --> 00:13:49,787
a woman came into your life

118
00:13:49,870 --> 00:13:53,082
when you were heartbroken?

119
00:13:54,542 --> 00:13:55,668
And then,

120
00:13:56,502 --> 00:13:57,878
she saved you?

121
00:13:58,462 --> 00:13:59,296
Yes.

122
00:14:00,214 --> 00:14:01,048
But

123
00:14:02,299 --> 00:14:04,385
the way you're saying it
makes it sound really bad.

124
00:14:04,468 --> 00:14:05,719
It's not like that!

125
00:14:05,803 --> 00:14:07,221
Because it really is bad!

126
00:14:07,304 --> 00:14:10,057
But, okay, I met her abroad!

127
00:14:11,016 --> 00:14:12,768
I met her abroad!

128
00:14:15,563 --> 00:14:16,647
<i>Alice.</i>

129
00:14:18,023 --> 00:14:19,316
Alice.

130
00:14:22,903 --> 00:14:25,364
Alice, Alice.

131
00:14:25,447 --> 00:14:27,032
<i>Alice.</i>

132
00:14:27,116 --> 00:14:28,367
<i>That day,</i>

133
00:14:29,702 --> 00:14:30,828
<i>I thought my life was over.</i>

134
00:14:34,373 --> 00:14:38,168
<i>But because of her, I found hope again.</i>

135
00:14:51,974 --> 00:14:55,895
So don't think that just because
La Morte Bianca is gone

136
00:14:55,978 --> 00:14:58,105
La Concordat is over.

137
00:14:58,731 --> 00:15:01,817
That's not how these organizations work.

138
00:15:02,401 --> 00:15:06,071
When one falls, someone takes their place.

139
00:15:06,155 --> 00:15:07,448
And more often than not,

140
00:15:08,240 --> 00:15:09,742
they're even more dangerous.

141
00:15:12,119 --> 00:15:14,872
If someone is making
a move around Mikoy and Chiara,

142
00:15:14,955 --> 00:15:16,749
we can't rule out

143
00:15:16,832 --> 00:15:19,668
that they're connected to La Concordat.

144
00:15:30,971 --> 00:15:33,933
Continue the profile, okay?

145
00:15:34,016 --> 00:15:37,102
<i>Find what we're missing.</i>

146
00:15:37,728 --> 00:15:39,313
Stay on high alert for now.

147
00:15:39,396 --> 00:15:42,191
No assumptions. We need facts.

148
00:15:48,489 --> 00:15:50,032
<i>And in the mafia,</i>

149
00:15:50,783 --> 00:15:54,954
<i>the fight for the throne never truly ends.</i>

150
00:15:58,082 --> 00:15:59,291
So,

151
00:15:59,792 --> 00:16:01,210
where is she now?

152
00:16:03,253 --> 00:16:05,214
She went back to her hometown.

153
00:16:07,758 --> 00:16:09,009
But

154
00:16:09,635 --> 00:16:12,137
why did you have to make it so suspicious

155
00:16:12,221 --> 00:16:13,555
just by talking to her?

156
00:16:14,723 --> 00:16:17,559
And you even went as far
as switching SIM cards.

157
00:16:19,687 --> 00:16:22,147
Babe. You're an agent, right?

158
00:16:24,316 --> 00:16:27,403
You know there are people
who don't want to be traced.

159
00:16:28,278 --> 00:16:31,365
So when I found out
she was here, and she talked to me,

160
00:16:32,074 --> 00:16:33,534
I immediately started thinking.

161
00:16:34,410 --> 00:16:37,037
What if someone was monitoring my phone?

162
00:16:37,121 --> 00:16:39,164
And I didn't want her
to get dragged into it.

163
00:16:40,499 --> 00:16:43,460
So I immediately bought a prepaid SIM.

164
00:16:43,544 --> 00:16:46,755
Then after one call,
I threw it straight in the trash.

165
00:16:46,839 --> 00:16:48,382
Just a safety precaution.

166
00:16:55,014 --> 00:16:57,057
I guess you're just being protective.

167
00:16:59,518 --> 00:17:02,730
I really am protective
of the people I love.

168
00:17:03,355 --> 00:17:04,690
And you're one of them.

169
00:17:12,239 --> 00:17:13,782
Let me make it up to you.

170
00:17:35,054 --> 00:17:38,932
<i>We confessed our feelings,</i>
<i>then we got married.</i>

171
00:17:39,433 --> 00:17:41,351
<i>So, are we officially together?</i>

172
00:17:42,102 --> 00:17:43,187
<i>Confession,</i>

173
00:17:43,270 --> 00:17:45,731
<i>fake wedding while drunk.</i>

174
00:17:45,814 --> 00:17:47,274
<i>Does that count?</i>

175
00:17:50,194 --> 00:17:54,490
<i>We can't just suddenly</i>
<i>become boyfriend and girlfriend, right?</i>

176
00:17:55,824 --> 00:17:58,619
<i>Or maybe we need to go</i>
<i>on a honeymoon first?</i>

177
00:17:59,203 --> 00:18:02,414
<i>Oh, Sofie, you're getting ahead</i>
<i>of yourself again!</i>

178
00:18:38,784 --> 00:18:43,497
What's the proper message
to send after a wedding?

179
00:18:45,332 --> 00:18:46,792
Is there etiquette for that?

180
00:18:49,044 --> 00:18:50,129
Okay.

181
00:18:54,466 --> 00:18:55,300
No.

182
00:19:07,646 --> 00:19:11,692
She might think I'm serious
about marrying her.

183
00:19:13,110 --> 00:19:14,027
Wait.

184
00:19:15,737 --> 00:19:17,531
Am I serious?

185
00:19:19,199 --> 00:19:23,787
<i>Maybe he's just embarrassed,</i>
<i>or maybe he was really just drunk.</i>

186
00:19:25,664 --> 00:19:27,499
No, whatever.

187
00:19:30,294 --> 00:19:32,171
Oh, no. Oh, no, it sent!

188
00:19:49,730 --> 00:19:51,815
Good thing I'm out of load.

189
00:20:20,969 --> 00:20:23,805
Some information came in at the agency.

190
00:20:23,889 --> 00:20:25,098
It's not verified yet,

191
00:20:25,599 --> 00:20:28,894
so I can't give you the details.

192
00:20:29,728 --> 00:20:31,897
But it's enough

193
00:20:31,980 --> 00:20:35,525
for me to tell you to keep an eye
on your surroundings for now.

194
00:20:36,276 --> 00:20:37,986
Is this about Chiara and the others?

195
00:20:38,570 --> 00:20:42,950
For now, I can't say yes,
but I can't say no either.

196
00:20:44,117 --> 00:20:46,453
I'm just keeping my promise.

197
00:20:47,037 --> 00:20:48,205
Thank you.

198
00:20:48,288 --> 00:20:51,083
And Mario, until we're sure,

199
00:20:52,709 --> 00:20:56,964
let's just let them think
it's only about the wedding.

200
00:20:57,547 --> 00:20:59,299
Okay, you're right.

201
00:20:59,841 --> 00:21:01,760
I'll handle things here.

202
00:21:14,815 --> 00:21:16,775
Fire! There's a fire!

203
00:21:16,858 --> 00:21:18,110
- Fire!
- Mario!

204
00:21:18,193 --> 00:21:19,987
- Mario!
- Mario!

205
00:21:20,070 --> 00:21:22,322
- Mario!
- Mario!

206
00:21:22,406 --> 00:21:24,491
- Mario, there's a fire!
- Mario!

207
00:21:24,574 --> 00:21:26,451
- Mario!
- Mario!

208
00:21:26,535 --> 00:21:27,369
- Come on, hurry.
- Let's go.

209
00:21:28,453 --> 00:21:29,496
Mario!

210
00:21:31,957 --> 00:21:33,208
Straight ahead!

211
00:22:14,249 --> 00:22:15,709
<i>How are you?</i>

212
00:22:17,794 --> 00:22:19,880
Unfortunately, still alive.

213
00:22:21,465 --> 00:22:23,800
Sometimes, that's enough.

214
00:22:24,426 --> 00:22:26,887
When we lose someone,

215
00:22:28,096 --> 00:22:30,182
we only have two choices.

216
00:22:30,682 --> 00:22:33,518
We can choose to follow them,

217
00:22:34,102 --> 00:22:37,189
or we can live with a purpose.

218
00:22:38,732 --> 00:22:40,067
Even now,

219
00:22:42,319 --> 00:22:44,654
I feel like everything is my fault.

220
00:22:46,698 --> 00:22:48,408
I couldn't save her.

221
00:22:50,660 --> 00:22:53,205
If only I had been braver.

222
00:22:56,333 --> 00:22:58,752
I wish Alice were still with me.

223
00:22:59,419 --> 00:23:02,214
I know what it's like to lose someone.

224
00:23:02,964 --> 00:23:05,217
But you know what's even more painful?

225
00:23:07,302 --> 00:23:10,889
Living your life without doing anything.

226
00:23:14,518 --> 00:23:16,186
For the rest of your life,

227
00:23:17,896 --> 00:23:20,941
we slowly give up.

228
00:23:21,900 --> 00:23:23,193
But they,

229
00:23:23,693 --> 00:23:25,737
they just keep living.

230
00:23:26,488 --> 00:23:28,573
They just keep hurting people.

231
00:23:31,576 --> 00:23:32,911
What else can I do?

232
00:23:34,246 --> 00:23:35,455
A lot.

233
00:23:36,039 --> 00:23:38,458
Don't waste your pain.

234
00:23:39,751 --> 00:23:40,919
Use it.

235
00:23:41,837 --> 00:23:44,548
Make it your reason to fight.

236
00:23:47,050 --> 00:23:49,010
And if I want

237
00:23:49,719 --> 00:23:54,432
to find whoever did this to Alice and me?

238
00:23:55,433 --> 00:23:57,936
You don't have to do this alone.

239
00:23:58,562 --> 00:24:00,063
I'll be with you.

240
00:24:00,647 --> 00:24:02,649
Let's help each other.

241
00:24:03,984 --> 00:24:06,278
While you seek justice,

242
00:24:08,280 --> 00:24:10,240
I'll help you learn to live again.

243
00:24:18,456 --> 00:24:21,251
Let's fill the emptiness with new reasons

244
00:24:21,334 --> 00:24:23,253
to live and fight.

245
00:24:42,814 --> 00:24:45,650
- because of the severity of his injuries.
- Injuries?

246
00:24:45,734 --> 00:24:46,693
<i>How is he?</i>

247
00:24:46,776 --> 00:24:49,112
We still don't know if there was a fight

248
00:24:49,196 --> 00:24:51,364
or if he violated any rules inside.

249
00:24:54,659 --> 00:24:55,744
Not far.

250
00:24:55,827 --> 00:24:57,871
This is starting to feel
like a security agency!

251
00:24:58,455 --> 00:24:59,289
How are you related to him?

252
00:24:59,372 --> 00:25:01,166
- He's my brother.
- All right. You're good, bro-in-law!

253
00:25:01,249 --> 00:25:02,959
Could there be a reason for it?

254
00:25:03,501 --> 00:25:04,794
They're not like this before.

255
00:25:11,676 --> 00:25:12,677
Here's the thing.

256
00:25:12,761 --> 00:25:16,139
Do you think if Victor escaped,
he'd come back?

257
00:25:16,223 --> 00:25:18,183
I'm just worried. Something's not right.

258
00:25:18,266 --> 00:25:22,687
And we both know that Senator Quintin
is up to something dirty.

259
00:25:25,273 --> 00:25:26,816
I was just thinking.

260
00:25:28,652 --> 00:25:30,987
What if we don't go through
with the wedding?
